# Total connectivity (silence is a defect)

**SYSTEM-WIDE (owner 2026-07-22):** Deep linkage is the **entire product** — Safety, Compliance, Fleet/Vehicles, Trailers, Dispatch, Settlements, Escrow, Banking, Accounting, Maintenance, Insurance, Legal, Drivers — **not** Insurance Claims / Legal only. Claims A2 is a depth *sample*; every module gets the same bar. No stone left unturned.

Before any block, declare: canonical target table (`to_regclass`, NOT a RETIRE table), the cross-module linkage matrix, and deployed SHA vs origin/main.
- **Never write/FK a RETIRE table:** `driver_finance.*` (not payroll/settlement) · `mdata.qbo_*` (not accounting.qbo_*) · `banking.*` (not bank.*) · `maintenance.*` (not maint.*) · `mdata.vendors` · `mdata.loads` · `catalogs.cancellation_reasons`. Verify the canonical exists on prod before repointing.
- Every record links BOTH-WAY to its financial primitives AND operational modules AND the hub tables (org.companies, identity.users, mdata.drivers/units/loads/customers/vendors, catalogs.accounts, maintenance.work_orders, accounting.journal_entries). A block with no linkage declaration is a defect.
- C1–C9 apply. Entity-scope every link (`operating_company_id` + FORCED RLS; cross-entity FK = defect). Wiring is part of the build (migration + backfill 0-NULL + route mounted + component reachable + guard wired). Additive only; guards only add. Enforced by CI guards G1–G4.
